/ROUTINE TO ADJUST THE X TABLE VALUES

/THE VALUE TO BE ADJUSTED IS IN THE <AC>

XADJUS,	.-.			/SUBROUTINE HEADER
	DCA	ADJTM1		/STORE THE <AC> IN A TEMPORARY
	TAD	ADJTM1		/GET THE VALUE TO BE ADJUSTED
	MQL			/LOAD THE MQ
	IFNZRO	DECMATE <
	CIF 	CDFL1		/CHANGE TO FIELD WHERE EAE IS LOCATED
	>
	MUY			/LOAD IT INTO THE MQ AND
XQUOT,	.-.			/MULTIPLY 
	SWP			/GET THE PRODUCT
	DCA	ADJTM2		/STORE IT IN ANOTHER TEMPORARY
	TAD	ADJTM1		/GET THE VALUE TO BE ADJUSTED
	MQL			/LOAD THE MQ
	IFNZRO	DECMATE <
	CIF 	CDFL1		/CHANGE TO FIELD WHERE EAE IS LOCATED
	>
	MUY			/LOAD IT INTO THE MQ AND
XREMAIN,.-.			/MULTIPLY
	IFNZRO	DECMATE <
	CIF 	CDFL1		/CHANGE TO FIELD WHERE EAE IS LOCATED
	>
	DVI			/AND THEN DIVIDE 
	6			/BY 6
	JMS I	(ROUND)		/ROUND THE REMAINDER 
	SWP			/GET THE QUOTIENT
	TAD	ADJTM2		/ADD THE CONTENTS OF THE SECOND TEMPORARY
	JMP I	XADJUS		/RETURN LEAVING THE ANSWER IN THE <AC>

/ROUTINE TO ADJUST THE Y TABLE VALUES

